# Frontend design system

- **Files:** `saa-s-frontend-build/frontend/globals.css` is the single source for marketing/customer-facing semantic tokens and frontend-only utilities (patterns, diagonal/grid backgrounds).
- **Tone:** High clarity, brand gold/primary, optional gradients and illustration-friendly spacing. Shadows may use `--shadow-md` / `--shadow-lg`.
- **Do not** import `admin/globals.css` or reuse admin-only neutrals here.
- When adding UI under `app/(site)/`, use token-mapped classes; extend `frontend/globals.css` if a new semantic is needed across many screens.

## Typography and color (important)

- Root layout uses `<html class="dark">`. Shadcn primitives (`Input`, `Select`, `Label`) use `text-foreground` / `text-popover-foreground`, which are **light** in dark mode.
- **Light “form pages”** (white fields, gray page background): wrap the page shell in **`className="light"`** on `<main>` or a top-level div. `frontend/globals.css` defines `html.dark .light { … }` so semantic tokens match `:root` (dark body copy on light surfaces).
- **Radix Select dropdowns** render in a **portal** (sibling of your wrapper), so they **do not** inherit `.light`. For any `SelectContent` on a light form under `html.dark`, add **`frontend-select-content-light`** to `className` so popover/accent tokens stay readable.
- Prefer **`text-gray-900`** for primary field labels and values on white; use **`text-gray-600`** / **`text-gray-500`** for helper and secondary text. Reserve **`text-[#D4AF37]`** (or `text-primary`) for brand accents and CTAs.
